>
>This one is tricky. Firstly, make sure you are using the latest milo, which is
>probably available from gatekeeper.dec.com in /pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels as
>ldmilo-ruffian-981020 and milo-ruffian-981020 (rename to ldmilo.exe and milo on
>whatever media you are loading it from).
>
>This may or may not fix the problem. If it does, then well and good. If it
>doesn't, try limiting the amount of memory the kernel sees to 224M (set
>MEMORY_SIZE 224 at the milo prompt). If that fixes it, then the bug regarding
>ruffians using more than 224M of memory may still exist. If it doesn't then the
>problem presumably lies elsewhere.
